WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.824
The choir leader came over to Rat.

2
00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:06.731
"Can I help you, sir?" said the mouse.

3
00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:09.190
Rat spoke quietly.

4
00:00:09.191 --> 00:00:12.270
"Are the shops still open?" he asked.

5
00:00:12.271 --> 00:00:14.771
The mouse nodded politely.

6
00:00:14.772 --> 00:00:18.592
"Shops are open late this time of year," he said.

7
00:00:18.593 --> 00:00:22.636
Rat put some coins into the mouse's paw.

8
00:00:22.637 --> 00:00:24.897
"Great!" said Rat.

9
00:00:24.898 --> 00:00:30.192
"Go buy us some good food."

10
00:00:30.193 --> 00:00:33.765
The rest of the mice sat down by the fire.

11
00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:37.093
Mole was opening his empty cupboards.

12
00:00:37.094 --> 00:00:41.186
"Oh dear," Mole said, shaking his head.

13
00:00:41.187 --> 00:00:46.690
"Now," cried Rat, "what shall we do for fun?"

14
00:00:46.691 --> 00:00:49.823
Mole turned and looked at Rat.

15
00:00:49.824 --> 00:00:54.737
"Well," said Mole, "these mice are actors too.

16
00:00:54.738 --> 00:00:58.190
They did a play about pirates last year."

17
00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:03.235
"Really? Let's see!" cried Rat.

18
00:01:03.236 --> 00:01:06.140
The mice whispered together.

19
00:01:06.141 --> 00:01:09.825
"Samuel should do it," said one, pointing.

20
00:01:09.826 --> 00:01:13.929
"Yes, Sammy will do it!" said the others.

21
00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:17.448
One young mouse stood shyly.

22
00:01:17.449 --> 00:01:20.482
"Say something from the play," said Rat.

23
00:01:20.483 --> 00:01:23.022
"Ahem," said Samuel.

24
00:01:23.023 --> 00:01:25.715
"Go on," said Mole.

25
00:01:25.716 --> 00:01:29.326
"Don't be shy," said Rat.

26
00:01:29.327 --> 00:01:34.089
"Um, um . . . ," Samuel said.

27
00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:37.001
The other mice encouraged him.

28
00:01:37.002 --> 00:01:40.222
"You can do it, Sammy!" they said.

29
00:01:40.223 --> 00:01:45.521
"Um, um," the young mouse repeated.

30
00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:48.734
"Here now, little one," said Rat.

31
00:01:48.735 --> 00:01:51.019
"Everyone is waiting."

32
00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:55.369
"Oh Rat," said Mole, "give him a chance."

33
00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:59.810
Suddenly the door flew open.

